⭐ NON-VACUITY: the instrument must be shown able to report a non-zero
   sig_wait_ms at all before any zero means anything. The 5 s probe window makes
   zeros the common case by design. Assert a non-zero reading is possible — e.g.
   two threads calling _current_version() with a stubbed slow _data_signature()
   in a unit test — or the field is decoration and an all-zeros session reads as
   "the lock is innocent" when it may mean "the field never worked".

=== WHY NOT JUST SHIP THE ONE-LINE FIX ===

Because it would be the sixth speculative fix on a thread that has already paid
for five, and it would be unfalsifiable afterwards: if handoffs improve, nobody
can say whether this was the cause; if they do not, nobody can say whether the
mechanism is wrong or merely secondary. The instrument makes it answerable.
